            <ArticleTitle>Phenotypic approach to the management of the chronic prostatitis/chronic pelvic pain syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1252-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1464-410X.2010.09701.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>• Our traditional approach to managing the chronic prostatitis (CP) syndromes has not been very successful for many of our patients. • Our developing understanding of CP/chronic pelvic pain syndrome (CP/CPPS) as a heterogeneous syndrome rather than a homogenous disease has allowed us to develop treatment strategies based on individual patient characteristics. • By considering each patient as a unique individual and tailoring treatments to a specific patient's clinical 'phenotype' we improve our therapeutic outcomes.</AbstractText>
